  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 12-layer alternating ZnS/ZnSe stack on Ge substrate at normal incidence. Layers 1-2 and 11-12 frozen at thicknesses 417 nm (ZnS) and 455 nm (ZnSe) respectively. Layers 3-10 optimizable with thickness bounds 500-1500 nm, initialized with Gaussian distribution centered at 750 nm with standard deviation 5 nm. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with learning rate 0.015 (half of previous 0.03). Spectral range 3000-11000 nm sampled at 2001 points. Maximize transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band while minimizing transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. Coherent TMM solver. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 12-layer alternating ZnS/ZnSe dielectric stack on a germanium substrate at normal incidence using coherent transfer-matrix theory. Freeze outer pairs (layers 1-2 and 11-12) at 417 nm and 455 nm respectively. Optimize inner eight layers (3-10) within 500-1500 nm thickness bounds initialized at 750 nm. Maximize average transmittance in the 8000-11000 nm band and minimize average transmittance in the 3000-5000 nm band across 2001 spectral points.",
